---
import CourseHome from '../../../../components/course/CourseHome.astro';
import { STARTUP } from '../../../../courses/startup/syllabus';
import '../../../../styles/lesson-kit.css';
---
<CourseHome course={STARTUP}>
  <section class="cs-builds">
    <h2>What you will be able to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Test an idea cheaply</strong>: find a real problem, talk to customers, price it and work out break-even and runway.</li>
      <li><strong>Pick the right legal shape</strong>: sole proprietor, partnership, LLP, LLC or company, and where to register it.</li>
      <li><strong>Become official</strong> in India, Canada or the USA: name checks, registration, tax numbers, licences and a bank account.</li>
      <li><strong>Handle tax</strong>: GST, HST and US sales tax, income tax for each structure, paying yourself, and the yearly deadlines.</li>
      <li><strong>Build a team</strong>: hire and run payroll, split equity, vest it, and write a co-founder agreement.</li>
      <li><strong>Protect and grow</strong>: trademarks, contracts, privacy laws, annual filings, and how to expand or close properly.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Pick your country with the switch at the top of every lesson; shared ideas are written once and the rules for India, Canada and the USA sit side by side. Every rule links to the government page it comes from and says the date it was checked. Each lesson has an interactive tool or step-by-step flow, a worked example, practice questions, a quiz and, where useful, a checklist you can tick and download.</p>
    <p class="cs-small">This course explains the law in plain words; it is not legal or tax advice. Rules change and every business is different, so check the official source and talk to a lawyer, chartered accountant or CPA before you act.</p>
  </section>
</CourseHome>
